.\" Manual page for the mdn daemon. @VERSION@ and @DATE@ are filled in by
.\" whichever route installs it, so the footer names the version that route
.\" shipped (davison/md-notes#168):
.\"
.\"   - `make build` writes ./mdn.1 from this file, and `make install` installs
.\"     that at $(PREFIX)/share/man/man1/mdn.1.gz;
.\"   - packaging/deb/build.sh stages it for the .deb, at the same path;
.\"   - the AUR package's PKGBUILD downloads it from the release's tag and fills
.\"     it in during package(), and makepkg compresses it to the same path.
.\"
.\" It lived in packaging/deb/ until then, which is how the other two routes
.\" came to leave it out: it looked like part of the Debian packaging rather
.\" than part of the program.
.\"
.\" It was first written because Debian Policy 12.1 asks every program in
.\" /usr/bin for one, and lintian says so (davison/md-notes#137); the
.\" alternative was a lintian override justifying its absence, and for a
.\" command with four subcommands the page is smaller than the justification.
.\"
.\" Every flag and every configuration key below was read off cmd/mdn/*.go and
.\" internal/config/config.go rather than from memory. A manual page installed
.\" into /usr/share/man is the same class of claim as a comment or a README
.\" line, and this milestone has a requirement about those being true.
.TH MDN 1 "@DATE@" "md-notes @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdn \- local markdown notes served to a browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdn serve
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mdn open
.RI [ options ]
.I DIR
.br
.B mdn token
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mdn version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdn
is a small local service that turns folders of markdown files into a notes
application in the browser, and doubles as a markdown viewer for any folder on
disk.
It renders notes server\-side, watches the configured roots for changes made by
other tools, searches them with
.BR rg (1),
and pushes changes to the open page over Server\-Sent Events.
.PP
It listens on the loopback address.
A
.B tailnet_host
may be configured so that the daemon also answers to one extra Host name
forwarded by a
.B tailscale serve
proxy; every request under that name must authenticate.
.PP
Notes stay plain markdown files in a folder hierarchy, editable with any tool
and synced by anything that syncs files.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the daemon against the configured roots: the notes root, where clips land,
and any permanent roots after it.
This is what the systemd user unit starts.
Every start logs each root it serves with its slug, kind and path.
.TP
.BI "open " DIR
Register
.I DIR
with the running daemon as a recent root and open it in the browser.
Roots added this way are remembered in the state file; there is no verb that
removes one, and the home page is where that is done.
.TP
.B token
Print the daemon's bearer token, which the browser extension needs.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.SH OPTIONS
Each option is also accepted with two leading dashes.
.SS mdn serve
.TP
.BI \-config " FILE"
Configuration file.
Default
.IR ~/.config/mdn/config.yml .
.TP
.BI \-root " DIR"
A folder to serve.
Repeat it for several: the first is the notes root and the rest are permanent
roots, in the order given.
Any
.B \-root
replaces
.B notes_root
from the configuration file completely rather than adding to it, and the start
logs the roots it set aside.
Two roots naming the same folder, including through a symlink, stop the daemon
at startup.
.TP
.BI \-port " N"
Loopback port, overriding
.B port
in the configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-state " FILE"
File that remembers the roots added with
.BR "mdn open" .
.TP
.BI \-token\-file " FILE"
File holding the bearer token clients present.
Created on first start.
.TP
.BI \-max\-watches " N"
Directories watched per root for live update;
.B 0
for no limit.
Overrides
.B max_watches
in the configuration file.
Default 8192.
.TP
.BI \-tailnet\-host " NAME"
Extra Host name to answer to, for a
.B tailscale serve
proxy.
Overrides
.B tailnet_host
in the configuration file.
.SS mdn open
.TP
.BI \-config " FILE"
Configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-port " N"
Daemon port, overriding
.B port
in the configuration file.
.TP
.B \-no\-browser
Print the URL instead of opening a browser.
.SS mdn token
.TP
.BI \-token\-file " FILE"
File holding the daemon's bearer token.
.TP
.B \-rotate
Replace the token with a new one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mdn/config.yml
The daemon's configuration:
.BR notes_root ,
.BR port ,
.BR max_watches ,
.B clips_dir
and
.BR tailnet_host .
.B notes_root
takes one path or a list of them.
The first entry is the notes root and the rest are permanent roots, in the
order given; each must be an existing directory.
.RS
.PP
.nf
notes_root:
  \- /home/you/notes
  \- /home/you/projects
.fi
.RE
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mdn/roots.json
The recent roots, added with
.B mdn open
or by the browser extension, with their slugs, so they survive a restart.
The notes root and permanent roots are configuration: the daemon never adds them
here.
A recent root whose folder is now configured is served once, as configured, and
its entry stays in this file, so a start without that configuration serves it
as a recent root again, under its old slug.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mdn/token
The bearer token clients present, created on first start.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/mdn.service
The systemd user unit, where the packages and a default
.B make install
put it.
Under another
.BR PREFIX ,
.B make install
puts it under that prefix instead, and it then needs a drop\-in pointing
.B ExecStart
at the binary, as the unit's header describes.
Start it with
.RS
.PP
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now mdn
.fi
.RE
.PP
The first three paths above follow
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME " and " XDG_STATE_HOME
where those are set; the defaults are shown.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
The daemon shells out to
.BR rg (1)
to list and to search a root.
Without ripgrep the navigator is empty and search returns nothing, which is why
the packages depend on it and a source install needs it on
.BR PATH .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rg (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
The full documentation is at
.UR https://github.com/davison/md-notes
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Darren Davison
